# Obsidian Vault — Claude Workflow Instructions

This is an Obsidian vault initialized for the daily-session / checkpoint / end-day workflow. Any Claude session launched inside this directory should treat these as the operating conventions.

---

## Layout

```
<vault-root>/
├── local/
│   ├── journals/              # One markdown file per day (YYYY-MM-DD.md) + _open-threads.md
│   ├── daily-gn/              # Daily wrap-up summaries; .tracking/ holds JSONL hook output
│   ├── ai-chats/
│   │   ├── transcripts/       # Daily session transcripts: YYYY-MM-DD/daily-session-YYYY-MM-DD.md
│   │   └── claude-code/       # Cross-session Claude Code export summaries
│   ├── templates/             # Obsidian templates (Daily Journal Template.md, etc.)
│   └── local-projects/        # Personal scratch projects
├── .claude-vault.json         # Vault marker (read by the workflow hooks for auto-detect)
└── CLAUDE.md                  # This file
```

All workflow content lives under `local/`. Treat that as the writable tree. Do not write workflow output anywhere else in the vault.

---

## Primary commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `/daily-session` | Start a new daily session — reads previous handoff, creates today's transcript, adds an entry to the daily note. `--light` skips file creation. |
| `/checkpoint [note]` | Timestamped checkpoint in the active transcript. Increments checkpoint count in daily note. `--archive` also exports the full conversation to `archives/`. |
| `/daily-resume` | Read-only catch-up for a fresh window mid-day — ingests today's transcript/journal/open-threads and replies with a goal-progress table. |
| `/end-day [--date YYYY-MM-DD]` | Wraps the session — generates Session Handoff inside the transcript, updates daily note, updates `_open-threads.md`, compiles the daily wrap-up summary. Auto-detects late-night sessions. |

The full daily loop: `/daily-session` → work happens → `/checkpoint` at logical breakpoints (+ `/daily-resume` in any new window) → `/end-day`.

---

## Canonical references

- **`local/journals/_open-threads.md`** is the source of truth for in-flight work + waiting-for asks. Update it FIRST, then let the daily journal mirror a snapshot. `/end-day` writes to this doc before finalizing the handoff.
- **`local/templates/Daily Journal Template.md`** is the schema for a new daily journal page. The daily note for a given date should be created at `local/journals/YYYY-MM-DD.md` using this template.
- **`local/daily-gn/.tracking/YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl`** is the accumulating accomplishment log. The `track-accomplishment.sh` hook writes to it on checkpoints, commits, file creation, and skill runs. `/end-day` reads it when compiling the daily wrap-up.

---

## Writing conventions

- **Wikilinks** (`[[Name]]`) are the standard linking format. Use them liberally — between transcripts, between projects, into the open-threads doc, and to reference any persistent entity (project, person, concept).
- **Dates in filenames** use ISO format: `YYYY-MM-DD`.
- **Timestamps in transcript entries** use `~HH:MMam/pm` (with `~` prefix to indicate approximate).
- **Frontmatter** on rolling docs (`_open-threads.md`, daily transcripts) follows the schemas embedded in those files.

---

## What goes where

| Content | Path |
|---------|------|
| A thinking session for today | `local/ai-chats/transcripts/YYYY-MM-DD/daily-session-YYYY-MM-DD.md` |
| Today's journal page | `local/journals/YYYY-MM-DD.md` |
| Rolling threads + waiting-fors | `local/journals/_open-threads.md` |
| Daily wrap-up summary | `local/daily-gn/YYYY-MM-DD.md` |
| Accomplishment tracking JSONL | `local/daily-gn/.tracking/YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl` |
| Pre-compaction snapshot | `local/ai-chats/transcripts/YYYY-MM-DD/archives/session-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM-full.md` |
| Cross-session Claude Code exports | `local/ai-chats/claude-code/<project>/<session>-summary.md` |
| A personal scratch project | `local/local-projects/<project-name>/` |

---

## Notes for Claude sessions

- The workflow hooks (`~/.config/claude-code/hooks/`) detect this vault by walking up from CWD looking for `.claude-vault.json`. If you find yourself unsure where to write, check `pwd` first — you should be inside this vault's tree.
- If `_open-threads.md` doesn't exist when `/end-day` runs, recreate it from `~/.claude/skills/vault-init/assets/_open-threads.template.md`.
- Never write workflow output to sibling directories outside the vault. All journal/transcript/wrap-up output stays under `local/`.
